 "why": "NETHER-THEMES (2026-10-10): one full-length demo dungeon per nether theme, for the theme's own tests (tests/test_dungeon_nether_themes.py) and for the authors of the five nether dungeons. Each is the same 25-entry shape (about 30 rooms with the crossroads routes) (an entry, a three-way crossroads with a lit, a dark and a flooded way out and their signs, a court the ways rejoin in, a maze, a resources room with the nether seam, a safe room with a healer, a stand, a parkour, a dark room, a collapse bridge, a nest, a mini-boss, a puzzle, a vault, a habitat, an ambush gauntlet, the arena, the exit) with the theme's own Pokemon in the fights; shape_mix on; four variants. A fixture for tests, not a dungeon anyone plays: the nether dungeons are authored in data/dungeons.json later.",
